  "notes": "Cash basis governmental, accrual business-type. Governmental beginning/ending_cash are the fund balances rolled forward on p4 (958,420 -> 955,444); ending equals cash 931,959 + county treasurer 6,080 + restricted 18,913 - payroll liabilities 1,508. Property taxes 211,642 (p4) split using the County Treasurer Activity schedule (p13), whose total revenues collected equal it exactly (incl. commissions -1,854). Sales and other taxes 146,454 split using budget-schedule lines (p8): Sales tax 111,444 + Motor vehicle tax 28,235 + Other state receipts 6,775. Business-type from the proprietary statement (p6), single Utilities column; disbursements total 1,320,117 printed on the Statement of Activities (p2). Balance sheet: combined Statement of Net Position, Total column (p1), since the government-wide statement includes business-type capital assets and debt. Detail: utility schedules (Water, Sewer, Electric, Trash pp9-12, tie to the p6 totals) and the County Treasurer schedule; the all-funds budget comparison (p8) is combined governmental+utility and is not recorded (would double count the utility schedules); per user rule 2026-10-28 no statement lines were added for the governmental funds. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
